1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:07,988
 اَلْحَمْدَ لِلّهِ نَحْمَدُهُ وَنَسْتَعِينينُهُ وَنَسْتَغْفِرُهُ وَنَتُوْبُ اِلَيْه،

2
00:00:08,788 --> 00:00:13,115
وَنَعُوذُ بِاللهِ مِنْ شُرُورِ أَنْفُسِنَا وَمِنْ سَيِّئَاتِ أَعْمَالِنَا،

3
00:00:13,908 --> 00:00:18,627
مَنْ يَهْدِهِ اللهُ فَلاَ مُضِلَّ لَهُ، وَمَنْ يُضْلِلْ فَلاَ هَادِىَ لَهُ،

4
00:00:19,327 --> 00:00:23,828
وَأَشْهَدُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللهُ وَحْدَهُ لاَ شَرِيكَ لَهُ،

5
00:00:24,361 --> 00:00:31,070
وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهُ وَرَسُولُهُ صَل اللهِ عَلَيْهِ وَعَلى أله وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلّمَ وَبَعْد

6
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:42,942
As we all have heard، the topic which will be discussed tonight, is a topic which is from the center of our beliefs.

7
00:00:44,049 --> 00:00:48,096
It is a topic rooted in the Qur'an Allah's final revelation.

8
00:00:49,189 --> 00:00:56,667
It is a topic that begins with the beginning of revelation to Allah's Prophet, Ibrahim عليه السلام

9
00:00:57,481 --> 00:01:04,517
and continues until the day of judgment with the return of the Prophet Eesa عليه السلام,

10
00:01:05,262 --> 00:01:12,793
passing through the Qur'an and the Sunnah(سنۃ) and the Seerah(سیرۃ) of our Prophet, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ.

11
00:01:14,424 --> 00:01:19,037
It is a topic which cannot be separated from our testimony of faith.

12
00:01:19,743 --> 00:01:23,990
لا اله الا الله محمد الرسول الله

13
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:29,326
There is none worthy of worship but Allah and Muhammad ﷺ is the Messenger of Allah.

14
00:01:30,179 --> 00:01:37,146
It is a topic which is part of the cancer which the Muslims suffer from today.

15
00:01:38,039 --> 00:01:46,678
And it is a topic which, unless we find a cure for it, we will not find a cure for other ills that we suffer from.

16
00:01:47,691 --> 00:01:49,398
The topic is great indeed.

17
00:01:50,131 --> 00:01:54,183
The topic deserves a whole conference, not just merely a lecture,

18
00:01:55,363 --> 00:02:00,635
and the topic deserves people of knowledge and honor to discuss it.

19
00:02:01,588 --> 00:02:13,421
However we ask Allah عزوجل to assist us, in order that we may perhaps convey to our brothers and sisters some knowledge regarding this topic,

20
00:02:14,015 --> 00:02:20,561
even though we ourselves are not from those, who deserve to discuss a topic of this importance.

21
00:02:22,594 --> 00:02:32,714
In order to understand the situation in Palestine, one must begin with the matter of our faith, the essence of our belief, Tawheed(توحيد).

22
00:02:33,994 --> 00:02:39,228
For as we all know Allah عزوجل has created us for a noble purpose.

23
00:02:40,161 --> 00:02:47,577
Allah has created humanity and every single human being, indeed the jinns, for a great reason.

24
00:02:48,804 --> 00:02:52,142
وَمَا خَلَقْتُ الْجِنَّ وَ الْاِنْسَ اِلَّا لِیَعْبُدُوْنِ۝

25
00:02:53,049 --> 00:02:56,569
I have not created jinns nor human beings but to worship Me.

26
00:02:57,662 --> 00:03:05,868
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has sent His Messengers as ones giving glad tidings and warning for this purpose,

27
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:12,293
 وَ لَقَدْ بَعَثْنَا فِیْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ رَّسُوْلًا اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَ اجْتَنِبُوا الطَّاغُوْتَۚ

28
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:22,829
And We have sent to every single people a messenger, ordering that messenger to preach worship Allah alone and avoid the worship of a Tagoot(طاغوت),

29
00:03:23,496 --> 00:03:25,669
all that is worshiped besides Allah.

30
00:03:26,935 --> 00:03:31,185
And indeed Allah's revelation is centered upon this principle.

31
00:03:31,939 --> 00:03:38,912
Throughout the Qur'an, we find the command to worship Allah and to avoid the worship of others.

32
00:03:39,298 --> 00:03:45,610
  وَعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَ لَا تُشْرِكُوْا بِهٖ شَیْــٴًـا وَ قَضٰى رَبُّكَ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِیَّاهُ

33
00:03:47,836 --> 00:03:51,789
And worship Allah alone and avoid the worship of others with Him.

34
00:03:52,163 --> 00:03:56,498
And your Lord has decreed that you worship, only but Him; and so forth and so on.

35
00:03:56,518 --> 00:04:05,631
And in the Sunnah(سنۃ) likewise, we find that our Prophet, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ stressing this principle over and over.

36
00:04:06,051 --> 00:04:11,871
One day his companion Muaaz bin Jabal رضي الله عنه is riding behind him on a donkey

37
00:04:12,217 --> 00:04:14,851
and the Prophet ﷺ says,

38
00:04:14,884 --> 00:04:19,274
O Muaaz(معاذ)! Do you know, when Allah's right is upon the creation?

39
00:04:20,561 --> 00:04:23,371
Muaaz(معاذ) says Allah and His Messenger know best.

40
00:04:24,250 --> 00:04:36,153
The Prophet ﷺ responds that His right meaning, Allah is right upon His creation is that His creation worship Him alone and does not associate anything with Him.

41
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:45,109
And then the Prophet ﷺ asked Muaaz(معاذ), and do you know what is the creations right upon Allah if they do that?

42
00:04:45,829 --> 00:04:49,128
Muaaz(معاذ) replies Allah and His Messenger knows best.

43
00:04:49,528 --> 00:04:55,985
The Prophet ﷺ says; Their right upon Allah that Allah will not punish them, if they do that.

44
00:04:58,452 --> 00:05:01,288
This message of Tawheed(توحيد) for which We have been created,

45
00:05:02,368 --> 00:05:05,391
for which Allah سبحانه وتعالى has sent His messengers,

46
00:05:05,984 --> 00:05:08,462
for which Allah has sent down His scriptures,

47
00:05:09,008 --> 00:05:15,385
and upon which Allah will judge every human being on the Day of Judgment, is the issue of Palestine.

48
00:05:15,472 --> 00:05:17,525
It is an issue of Tawheed(توحيد) and Shirk(شرک).

49
00:05:18,658 --> 00:05:20,814
It is an issue of Eeman(ایمان) and Kufr(کفر).

50
00:05:22,181 --> 00:05:32,476
It is not an issue of nationalism or one race against another race, or one political philosophy against another political philosophy,

51
00:05:33,069 --> 00:05:35,362
but it is an issue of truth and falsehood.

52
00:05:36,128 --> 00:05:42,153
It is an issue that begins with the father of the prophets, humanity's third father,

53
00:05:42,418 --> 00:05:53,160
the Prophet Ibrahim عليه السلام continuing to our Prophet, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and concluding with the Prophet Eesa عليه السلام.

54
00:05:56,487 --> 00:06:02,838
And in order to understand this issue, we must understand one aspect of Tawheed(توحيد);

55
00:06:03,825 --> 00:06:11,553
and that is that Allah سبحانه وتعالى, like He is the creator, He also is the One, Who selects.

56
00:06:12,647 --> 00:06:14,593
As Allah سبحانه وتعالى says,

57
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:24,612
 وَ رَبُّكَ یَخْلُقُ مَا یَشَآءُ وَ یَخْتَارُؕ-مَا كَانَ لَهُمُ الْخِیَرَةُؕ-سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ وَ تَعٰلٰى عَمَّا یُشْرِكُوْنَ۝

58
00:06:25,458 --> 00:06:28,074
Allahسبحانه وتعالى in Surat-Ul-Qasas(سورۃ القصص) says;

59
00:06:28,894 --> 00:06:32,836
And your Lord creates what He wills and chooses,

60
00:06:33,154 --> 00:06:35,169
they have no choice in the matter.

61
00:06:35,916 --> 00:06:39,976
Glory be to Allah and exalted from that which they associate unto Him.

62
00:06:41,076 --> 00:06:47,722
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى, as He is the Creator, He is also the One, Who chooses and selects from His creation.

63
00:06:48,695 --> 00:06:55,730
He has selected from His creation that the angels live in the heavens above,

64
00:06:56,410 --> 00:07:03,557
and from the angels, He has selected Jibrail(جبرائیل) and Mikail(میکائیل) and Israfil علیہم السلام.

65
00:07:04,530 --> 00:07:12,880
He has selected from the creatures, on those who are upon earth human beings, and Has selected from the human beings, the prophets.

66
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:15,680
And selected from the prophets the messengers,

67
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:21,285
and selected from the messengers, those five messengers of resolute determination.

68
00:07:21,605 --> 00:07:23,079
  اُولُوا الْعَزْمِ مِنَ الرُّسُلِ

69
00:07:23,699 --> 00:07:35,581
 the prophets Noah عليه السلام and Ibrahim عليه السلام and Musa عليه السلام and Eesa Ibn-E-Maryam عليه السلام and our Prophet, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ.

70
00:07:36,108 --> 00:07:44,313
And from those five messengers, He has chosen His two Khalil(خلیل)s, Ibrahim(ابراھیم) and Muhammad صلی اللہ علیہما وسلمہ.

71
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:57,280
And likewise from humanity, indeed, from everything He has chosen the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and selected him to be the master of all human beings, the leader of all humanity,

72
00:07:57,533 --> 00:08:00,000
as the Prophet ﷺ has said;

73
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,589
 أنَا سَيِّدُ وَلَدِ آدَمَ وَلَا فَخْرَ

74
00:08:03,235 --> 00:08:09,355
I am the master or the best of the children of Adam(آدم) and I say this not, out of a statement of boast.

75
00:08:10,835 --> 00:08:14,163
Likewise Allah سبحانه وتعالى choses certain times.

76
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:23,743
In the week he has chosen the day of Al Jumua(جمعہ) as a day, when which we worship Him and remember His creation.

77
00:08:23,783 --> 00:08:30,273
For Allah سبحانه وتعالى created the heavens and the earth in six days, the final day being the day of Jumuaa(جمعہ)

78
00:08:30,713 --> 00:08:35,659
And it is the day in which He has created Adam, and it is the day in which the Day of Judgment will occur.

79
00:08:36,193 --> 00:08:39,322
So Allah has selected this day as the day of our weekly worship.

80
00:08:40,509 --> 00:08:45,052
And likewise, He has chosen amongst the months, four months that are holy months,

81
00:08:45,518 --> 00:08:49,198
Muharram(محرم) and Rajab(رجب) and Zul Qada(ذوالقعدہ) and Zul Hijja(ذوالحجہ).

82
00:08:50,038 --> 00:08:52,813
And He has also chosen amongst the months Ramadan(رمضان)

83
00:08:53,345 --> 00:08:59,052
as the month in which we fast and in the month which we worship Him, and in the month which He revealed the Qur'an.

84
00:08:59,574 --> 00:09:01,908
And among nights, He chose Lelat-Ul-Qadar(لیلۃ القدر).

85
00:09:03,654 --> 00:09:06,706
And likewise Allah سبحانه وتعالى has chosen places.

86
00:09:07,979 --> 00:09:13,920
He has selected places in which He has honored and has set up for His worship alone.

87
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,895
He chose the lands of Mecca,

88
00:09:18,342 --> 00:09:24,685
and in Mecca, He chose a certain Valley in which His house was erected for His worship, the Ka’aba(کعبہ).

89
00:09:26,332 --> 00:09:28,474
And He chose the lands of Medina.

90
00:09:28,914 --> 00:09:39,476
And in Medina, He chose a certain part between its two valleys, in which the Prophet's Masjid was erected صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم.

91
00:09:40,676 --> 00:09:45,292
And likewise, He chose the lands of Ash-Sham(الشام), the lands of Syria.

92
00:09:45,898 --> 00:09:50,832
And from there, He chose specifically a certain city Bait-Al Maqdas(بیت المقدس).

93
00:09:51,198 --> 00:09:58,407
And from there He chose a certain hill, upon which Allah decreed that another Masjid(مسجد) be built, Masjid-Al-Aqsa(اقصی).

94
00:10:00,087 --> 00:10:01,734
This is part of Tawheed(توحيد).

95
00:10:02,345 --> 00:10:12,564
And this is why Allah سبحانه وتعالى made it part of our religion that one cannot set out in a journey for worship, except to these three Masajid(مساجد).

96
00:10:14,451 --> 00:10:19,143
And the prayers in these Masajid(مساجد) are multiplied in terms of its reward,

97
00:10:20,523 --> 00:10:26,330
and there are certain etiquettes and certain rewards that are connected with these three Masajid(مساجد),

98
00:10:26,672 --> 00:10:29,619
which are not connected with any other place on earth.

99
00:10:31,018 --> 00:10:41,982
And so therefore, to separate Masjid-Al-Aqsa(مسجد الاقصی) from Mecca and Medina, it is as if to separate part of Islam from another part.

100
00:10:43,629 --> 00:10:45,429
We are an Ummah(امۃ) of Tawheed(توحيد).

101
00:10:46,042 --> 00:10:48,395
We are an Ummah(امۃ) which follows the prophets.

102
00:10:48,869 --> 00:10:56,195
Do you not see that the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, when he found the Jews fasting the day of Ashura (عاشورہ),

103
00:10:56,628 --> 00:10:58,648
he inquired what day is this?

104
00:10:58,901 --> 00:11:06,067
They said, this is a noble day in which Allah سبحانه وتعالى rescued Moses from Pharaoh.

105
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:12,059
What did the Prophet ﷺ said; We are more deserving of Moses then them.

106
00:11:13,659 --> 00:11:17,080
And likewise, Allah in the Qur'an has informed us, that

107
00:11:17,127 --> 00:11:26,982
the Prophet Ibrahim عليه السلام was neither a Jew nor a Christian, nor from the pagans, but he ever, he was a Muslim, a Hanif(حنیف),

108
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:30,225
and he was not from the pagans worshiping Allah alone.

109
00:11:30,829 --> 00:11:38,272
And Allah tells us that the one, who is closest to Ibrahim عليه السلام were his immediate followers, and this prophet and the believers,

110
00:11:38,312 --> 00:11:40,861
meaning the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ.

111
00:11:42,254 --> 00:11:48,903
And do you not see, how Eesa عليه السلام, when he returns at the end of time, he returns as a Messenger,

112
00:11:49,403 --> 00:11:53,130
but judging by the Qur'an and the Sunnah, not with a new Sharia(شریعہ),

113
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:58,100
not ruling by the law, which was sent down to him, of the Injeel(انجیل) or of the Torah(توراۃ),

114
00:11:58,366 --> 00:12:03,813
but rather, as the Prophet ﷺ said؛ As a just ruler in this Ummah(امۃ).

115
00:12:05,639 --> 00:12:12,588
So the Ummah(امۃ) of Muhammad ﷺ, we are the believers in all the revelation of Allah,

116
00:12:13,181 --> 00:12:16,194
and we are the believers in all the prophets of Allah.

117
00:12:17,734 --> 00:12:24,570
And so therefore to separate parts of the places, which Allah has honored through some of his prophets،

118
00:12:25,623 --> 00:12:30,946
is as if we were to believe in part of the message and disbelieve in part of the message,

119
00:12:31,571 --> 00:12:35,118
or believe in some of the messengers and disbelieve in the others of the messengers.

120
00:12:35,631 --> 00:12:40,687
Baitul Maqdas, is connected to Mecca and Medina and can never be separated from it.

121
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:47,679
And the evidences upon this from the Quran and the Sunnah(سنۃ) are very many, and likewise from history.

122
00:12:48,279 --> 00:12:54,254
And what we will do in the next few moments is review some of those evidences.

123
00:12:55,754 --> 00:13:03,206
Allah سبحانه وتعالى in the Quran in five passages informs us that these lands of Ash-Sham(الشام),

124
00:13:03,666 --> 00:13:10,464
these lands of Syria and Lebanon and Palestine and Jordan, are lands in which Allah سبحانه وتعالى has blessed.

125
00:13:11,430 --> 00:13:17,381
And in the passage which I think most of us are most familiar with, in where Allah سبحانه وتعالى opens up,

126
00:13:18,468 --> 00:13:21,527
starts Surat-Ul-Isra(سورۃ الاسراء), Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

127
00:13:21,814 --> 00:13:29,183
سُبْحٰنَ الَّذِیْۤ اَسْرٰى بِعَبْدِهٖ لَیْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْاَقْصَا الَّذِیْ بٰرَكْنَا حَوْلَهٗ

128
00:13:30,509 --> 00:13:43,390
Glory be to Allah, Who took His servant meaning the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, during a night journey from Masjid-Al-Haram from Mecca to Masjid-Al-Aqsa(مسجدالاقصی),

129
00:13:44,277 --> 00:13:47,499
regarding which we have blessed the surrounding lands.

130
00:13:49,572 --> 00:13:54,057
and the connection; there is also a deep lesson in this.

131
00:13:54,103 --> 00:13:59,763
Not only is Allah سبحانه وتعالى teaching us, or telling us an event of the Prophet ﷺ life,

132
00:14:00,443 --> 00:14:02,965
but as Shaykh Ul Islam Ibn Taymiyah(شَيْخُ الإِسْلَام اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّة) has said;

133
00:14:03,292 --> 00:14:07,345
This also tells us the history of the Ummah(امۃ) in this, there is a deeper meaning.

134
00:14:07,945 --> 00:14:14,537
For just like the message of Islam began in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, in Mecca,

135
00:14:14,883 --> 00:14:17,786
it will come at the end of time and be in Jerusalem.

136
00:14:19,059 --> 00:14:26,638
And just like the beginning of the Ummah(امۃ), just like Mecca is more preferred and beloved to Allah عزوجل than Jerusalem,

137
00:14:27,165 --> 00:14:36,930
likewise the first of the Ummah(امۃ), meaning the Prophet ﷺ, his companions are better than those, who will be at the end of time, even though they will be with the Prophet Eesa عليه السلام.

138
00:14:40,447 --> 00:14:51,163
And indeed in the Prophet Sunnah(سنۃ), we find many narrations in which the Prophet ﷺ has stressed the importance of Bait-Al-Maqdas(بیت المقدس).

139
00:14:52,979 --> 00:15:00,291
For example we find that the Prophet ﷺ has said in one Hadith(حدیث).

140
00:15:01,184 --> 00:15:07,790
The Hadith(حدیث) of Memoona(میمونہ), the freed slave woman of the Prophet ﷺ.

141
00:15:07,810 --> 00:15:09,276
This is reported by Imam Ahmed(امام احمد);

142
00:15:09,836 --> 00:15:17,122
She says; Oh Messenger of Allah, give us a Fatwa(فتوی); give us an answer regarding Bait-Al-Maqdas(بیت المقدس).

143
00:15:17,902 --> 00:15:22,758
So even though Sahabah(صحابہ) used to question the Prophet ﷺ regarding Bait-Al-Maqdas(بیت المقدس)'s importance.

144
00:15:22,804 --> 00:15:27,714
What did the Prophet ﷺ say, as reported by Imam Ahmad (امام احمد) in the Musnad(مسند) , he says;

145
00:15:28,114 --> 00:15:30,554
 ارض المحشر والمنشر

146
00:15:30,754 --> 00:15:35,956
It is the land where the people will be gathered, and the land of the resurrection.

147
00:15:37,776 --> 00:15:44,322
And then the Prophet ﷺ has said, come to it and pray there.

148
00:15:46,016 --> 00:15:49,847
For a prayer, there is like a thousand prayers anywhere else,

149
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:55,547
and the meaning is anywhere else, outside of Mecca, Masjid Haram(مسجد الحرام), and Masjid Nabawi(مسجد النبوی) in Madina,

150
00:15:56,435 --> 00:16:01,568
and then Memoona(میمونہ) said, and if I cannot reach Bait-Al-Maqdas(بیت المقدس), what should I do?

151
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:10,070
The Prophet ﷺ said, then give as an offering some oil by which you might light the Masjid(مسجد).

152
00:16:10,090 --> 00:16:18,225
In other words, in the old days, before the advent of electricity, they would take oil and they would burn torches in order to give light in the Masajid(مساجد).

153
00:16:18,305 --> 00:16:20,805
So here the Prophet ﷺ says to Memoona(میمونہ),

154
00:16:20,825 --> 00:16:29,282
if you cannot reach Bait-Al-Maqdas(بیت المقدس), then send some oil there, in order to beautify that house of Allah عزوجل, so the people may pray there.

155
00:16:29,582 --> 00:16:31,371
The people may recite the Qur'an there.

156
00:16:31,631 --> 00:16:33,797
The people may do other acts of worship there.

157
00:16:35,037 --> 00:16:36,344
